      "sample_index": 1,
      "text": "To find the 100th digit after the decimal point of the decimal representation of \\(\\frac{1}{7}\\), we first need to determine the decimal representation of \\(\\frac{1}{7}\\).\n\nLet's perform the division of 1 by 7:\n\n\\[\n1 \\div 7 = 0.142857142857\\ldots\n\\]\n\nWe observe that the decimal representation of \\(\\frac{1}{7}\\) is a repeating decimal with the repeating block \"142857\". This block has a length of 6 digits.\n\nTo find the 100th digit in this repeating sequence, we need to determine the position of the 100th digit within the repeating block. We do this by finding the remainder when 100 is divided by 6:\n\n\\[\n100 \\div 6 = 16 \\text{ remainder } 4\n\\]\n\nThe remainder is 4, which means that the 100th digit corresponds to the 4th digit in the repeating block \"142857\".\n\nThe repeating block \"142857\" consists of the digits 1, 4, 2, 8, 5, and 7. The 4th digit in this sequence is 2.\n\nTherefore, the 100th digit after the decimal point of the decimal representation of \\(\\frac{1}{7}\\) is \\(\\boxed{2}\\).",
